3 TOP 5 DEEP DIVES

#1 CineForge. This is the cleanest bridge yet between the scanner=E2=80=99s
RSI and autonomous-video lanes. It does not merely self-critique a
render: production trajectories are converted into bounded stage-local
policy patches and validated across stories. Privately/YouTube
implication: replace generic =E2=80=98make next video better=E2=80=99 memor=
y with
typed policy patches for hook, pacing, shot choice, narration, edit
and CTA. Smallest experiment: run 10 synthetic short-video tasks,
permit one stage-local patch per episode, hold out 3 tasks for
regression. Falsifier: learned patches overfit one topic/style and
fail held-out clips.

#2 ShareLock. Existing MCP scanners often reason per tool. ShareLock=E2=80=
=99s
mechanism means every tool description can be individually innocuous
while the set is dangerous. Privately must therefore evaluate the
capability/tool SET and changes to its composition. Smallest safe
experiment: benign synthetic fragments distributed across 3=E2=80=935 dummy
tool descriptions, test whether set-level scanner flags reconstructed
semantics without executing effects. Falsifier: composition signal is
indistinguishable from benign cross-tool context at acceptable FPR.

#3 cMCP. This advances the defence generation from =E2=80=98policy exists
outside the agent=E2=80=99 to =E2=80=98policy execution itself is remotely
attestable.=E2=80=99 For high-value/private agents, a signed receipt is
stronger if the verifier can establish which policy binary/bundle
actually made the decision. Experiment: same Cedar grant in software
mode vs TEE-backed mode; verify TRACE claims and deliberate
policy-bundle mismatch. Falsifier: operational cost/latency overwhelms
value outside regulated/high-value workflows.

#4 Cryptorefills agents. This is a concrete answer to what agentic
purchasing looks like when it leaves toy API calls: 10,500+ real-world
products, no account, two crypto rails, discovery through fulfillment.
Privately implication: a narrow money grant can produce a
physical/digital external effect. Experiment: browse-only catalog,
compute capability/effect graph for a hypothetical $5 eSIM purchase
without transacting. Falsifier: purchase flow still needs enough human
identity/interaction that autonomous authority is limited.

#5 GRASP. The key contribution is not another reflection loop; it is
an explicit hard regression budget on edits to reusable skills. This
should be imported directly into Privately=E2=80=99s RSI model: no
self-modification gets authority merely because it fixes the current
failure. Experiment: allow agent to propose one skill patch, evaluate
current failure + balanced historical probes, reject on any protected
regression. Falsifier: probe suite has too little coverage to predict
real regressions.

